# OnePick Tools

OnePick Tools is a Docker-deployed media toolbox. Current focus: parse shared media links, proxy single-file downloads, and archive multi-item results into ZIP files.

## Deploy

```bash
cd /opt/docker/onepick
docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate
```

Default exposed port:

```text
http://<dev-host>:3877
```

## Pages

- `/` — main parser UI
- `/config` — runtime status, parser status, Cookie status, recent history

## APIs

- `GET /api/health`
- `GET /api/runtime`
- `GET /api/self-test`
- `GET /api/tools`
- `GET /api/history?limit=50`
- `POST /api/inspect`
- `POST /api/parse`
- `GET /api/download?url=...&filename=...`
- `POST /api/archive`

## Cookies

Put Netscape-format cookies here when a platform requires login/captcha bypass:

```text
cookies/douyin.txt
cookies/xiaohongshu.txt
cookies/kuaishou.txt
```

The directory is mounted read-only into the container at `/app/cookies`.

## Data

Runtime history is persisted in:

```text
data/history.jsonl
```

It is trimmed by `HISTORY_MAX_LINES` in `docker-compose.yml`.

## Self test

From the host:

```bash
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:3877/api/self-test | python3 -m json.tool
```

From inside the container/project:

```bash
ONEPICK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000 npm run self-test
```

From host against published port:

```bash
ONEPICK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3877 docker compose exec onepick-tools npm run self-test
```

## Current dedicated parsers

- Douyin
- Xiaohongshu
- Kuaishou

Generic fallback uses `yt-dlp`.
